# ⚙️ Environment Variables

## Backend

Create the required environment variables:

```env
DATABASE_URL=jdbc:postgresql://your-neon-host/neondb?sslmode=require&channel_binding=require
DATABASE_USERNAME=your_database_username
DATABASE_PASSWORD=your_database_password

GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key

RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=your_razorpay_key_id
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=your_razorpay_key_secret

FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:5173
```

### Production

For production deployment:

```env
DATABASE_URL=your_neon_database_url
DATABASE_USERNAME=your_neon_username
DATABASE_PASSWORD=your_neon_password

GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key

RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=your_razorpay_key_id
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=your_razorpay_key_secret

FRONTEND_URL=https://razorai-frontend.onrender.com
```

> **Never commit API keys, database passwords, or Razorpay secrets to GitHub.**

---

# 💻 Run Locally

## 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Rakeshpavanmudidana/razorai.git
cd razorai
```

## 2. Start the backend

```bash
cd backend
mvn spring-boot:run
```

Backend runs on:

```text
http://localhost:8080
```

## 3. Start the frontend

Open another terminal:

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

Frontend runs on:

```text
http://localhost:5173
```

---

# 🐳 Docker

The backend includes a Dockerfile for deployment.

Build the backend image:

```bash
docker build -t razorai-backend ./backend
```

Run:

```bash
docker run -p 8080:8080 razorai-backend
```

The application reads production configuration through environment variables.

